---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: /home/alice/.password-store is not a pass store, so none of the 3 mapping(s) declared
against it was read and nothing was written.

The refusal is here rather than after the first mapping deliberately: a run
that treated an absent store as an empty one would report every mapping as
one-sided and, in backup mode, write.

A store is a directory carrying a .gpg-id, which is the store's own
declaration of who can read it. Either the location is wrong:

    flake.safix.pass.store = "/home/<you>/.password-store";

or there is no store there yet, and creating one is yours rather than
safix's — writing a .gpg-id would be safix deciding who can read your
secrets:

    pass init <your-gpg-id>
